      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOUNDS OF PEACE (7) has been narrowly beaten as the favourite in both of her starts to date on this course, and as a slow-maturing 5YO mare, she is perfectly poised to go one better in this. JOEJOE (1) resumes from a spell, and has trialled up nicely twice in preparation for this. He is likely to be running on, and he can figure in the top 3. NINE CHOIRS (5) hit the line strongly last time out on this course over 1200m, following on from a very encouraging debut third by less than a length. The extra 200m is ideal, and she can take this out. SH'BOURNE RISING (6) did not get into it here 2 weeks ago over 1200m when looking for more ground. Stick with her for all combos. WOUNDED EAGLE (2) needed his resuming run and will have the blinkers on for the first time in this. Keep safe.",
